<h2 id="image-quality">Image Quality &amp; Style Control</h2>
<h3>Image Quality</h3>
<p>Firefly 3, Adobe's latest model, delivers exceptional image quality with photorealistic rendering, accurate lighting, and natural textures. The model excels at product photography, lifestyle imagery, and marketing materials. While it may not match Midjourney's artistic flair or DALL-E 3's creative interpretation, it prioritizes professional, usable results over artistic experimentation.</p>
<h3>Style Control</h3>
<p>Firefly offers extensive style control through multiple mechanisms:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Style Presets:</strong> Choose from dozens of artistic styles including Photo, Art, and Graphic presets</li>
<li><strong>Reference Images:</strong> Upload style and structure references to guide generation</li>
<li><strong>Detailed Prompting:</strong> Advanced prompt syntax for precise control over composition and elements</li>
<li><strong>In-Context Editing:</strong> Refine specific areas with Generative Fill for pixel-perfect results</li>
<li><strong>Color Grading:</strong> Apply color themes and adjust mood with built-in controls</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="commercial-rights">Commercial Usage Rights</h2>
<p>Adobe Firefly's most significant advantage is its commercial safety. Here's what you need to know:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>100% Commercially Safe Training:</strong> Trained only on Adobe Stock, public domain, and expired copyright content</li>
<li><strong>Full Commercial Rights:</strong> All generated images can be used commercially without attribution</li>
<li><strong>Content Credentials:</strong> Transparent metadata showing AI generation for ethical disclosure</li>
<li><strong>Enterprise Protection:</strong> Adobe indemnifies enterprise customers against copyright claims</li>
<li><strong>Brand Safety:</strong> Custom models ensure consistency with brand guidelines</li>
</ul>
<p>This makes Firefly the safest choice for businesses, agencies, and professionals who need legal certainty.</p>
<h2 id="prompt-engineering">Prompt Engineering</h2>
<h3>Writing Effective Prompts</h3>
<p>Firefly responds well to clear, descriptive prompts. Here are best practices:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Be Specific:</strong> "Modern minimalist kitchen with marble countertops and brass fixtures" works better than "nice kitchen"</li>
<li><strong>Include Style:</strong> Add style descriptors like "photorealistic," "watercolor," or "3D render"</li>
<li><strong>Specify Lighting:</strong> Mention lighting conditions like "golden hour," "studio lighting," or "soft diffused light"</li>
<li><strong>Set Composition:</strong> Indicate framing with "close-up," "wide angle," or "overhead view"</li>
<li><strong>Use References:</strong> Upload style or structure references for more consistent results</li>
</ul>
<h3>Advanced Techniques</h3>
<ul>
<li>Layer multiple style modifiers for unique looks</li>
<li>Use negative prompts to exclude unwanted elements</li>
<li>Combine Firefly generation with Photoshop editing for professional polish</li>
<li>Create variations to explore different interpretations</li>
</ul>
